# THE ACTIVATION FILE. Its presence is what authorizes paper order submission.
#
# Target: /etc/autotrader/autotrader.trading.env
#   owner  root:autotrader
#   mode   0640
#
# **Do not install this by hand, and do not let the deploy script create it.**
# It exists here as documentation of what activation actually consists of.
# `deploy/bin/autotrader-enable-paper-trading` is what writes it, and that
# script is the deliberate second action described in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md,
# "Deploy is not activation".
#
# On a freshly deployed host this file is ABSENT. The runtime units load it
# with a leading `-` (optional), so its absence is not an error - it simply
# leaves the safe defaults from autotrader.env standing, and the runtimes
# observe without an execution path.
#
# Deleting this file and restarting the runtimes returns the host to
# observe-only. That is what `autotrader-enable-paper-trading --disable` does.
#
# Note what is still NOT here: startup reconciliation reporting that trading
# is safe. That is the third gate, it is evaluated inside the runtime on every
# single start, and no file on disk can open it.

AUTOTRADER_PAPER_TRADING_ENABLED=true
AUTOTRADER_CRYPTO_ARGS=--confirm-paper-runtime PAPER
AUTOTRADER_EQUITY_ARGS=--confirm-paper-runtime PAPER
